.Dd June 17, 2026
.Dt ZDOTS-DOCTOR 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zdots-doctor
.Nd system health check for the zdots platform
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-runtime
.Op Fl q | Fl -quiet
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Dq brew doctor
for the workstation. It runs environment, repo, XDG-compliance, platform
version, AI-tool, services, and observability checks, then delegates the deep
runtime probe to
.Xr zdots-ctl 8
.Pq Cm check .
It also checks adots as a peer dependency. It exits 0 when no failures are
found and 1 on any
.Sy [FAIL] .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -no-runtime
Skip the
.Xr zdots-ctl 8
check section
.Pq fast mode; own sections only .
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Print only warnings and failures.
.It Fl -json
Emit results as JSON; the exit code reflects zdots-only status.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_O2_SIZE_WARN_GB
.It Ev ZDOTS_CONTEXT
.Li home
or
.Li work ;
gates PHI-posture checks
.Pq FileVault, AI mode .
.It Ev ZDOTS_O2_SIZE_WARN_GB
Threshold above which the Observability section warns of telemetry store drift.
Defaults to 8.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1
.It 0
No failures.
.It 1
One or more
.Sy [FAIL]
checks.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capabilities 1 ,
.Xr zdots-observability 7 ,
.Xr zdots-ctl 8
